{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ReebTowerJacobiAnger","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ReebTowerJacobiAnger","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_circle","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L105-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_growth_hyperbola","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_growth_hyperbola","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**The conic distinction.** The growth tower lives on the hyperbola\n`cosh²η − sinh²η = 1` (the `I_ν` world); the rotation tower lives on the circle\n`cos²θ + sin²θ = 1` (the `J_ν` world). Same recurrence, two conics — the\nelementary shadow of `I_ν(x) = i^{−ν} J_ν(i x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_abs_cos_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_abs_cos_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L93-L96","doc":"**Rotation regime (`J_ν`): the multiplier is bounded by `1`.** `|cos θ| ≤ 1`,\nso the rotation-tower recurrence multiplier `t = cos θ` lies in the bounded\n(`J_ν`, `arccos`) regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_growth_one_le_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_growth_one_le_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L87-L91","doc":"**Growth regime (`I_ν`): the multiplier is `≥ 1`.** `1 ≤ cosh η` always, so\nthe growth-tower recurrence multiplier `t = cosh η` lies in the unbounded\n(`I_ν`, `arccosh`) regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_sin_three_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_rotation_sin_three_term","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**Rotation (`J_ν`) analogue.** The *same* three-term recurrence holds for\n`sin` with multiplier `cos θ`: `sin(a+θ) + sin(a−θ) = 2 cos θ · sin a`. The\nrotation tower `sin(kθ)` and the growth tower `sinh(kη)` solve one operator\n`p_{k+1} = 2t·p_k − p_{k−1}`, with `t = cos θ` (`|t| ≤ 1`) vs `t = cosh η`\n(`t ≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_cosh_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_cosh_step","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The `cosh` recurrence form (bar-even sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_sinh_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_sinh_step","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L66-L71","doc":"**The recurrence form** `p(a+η) = 2 cosh η · p(a) − p(a−η)` for `p = sinh`.\nWith `a = kη`: `sinh((k+1)η) = 2 cosh η · sinh(kη) − sinh((k−1)η)` — the\nconstant-`k` three-term kernel (Chebyshev `U` / `q→1` Bessel contiguity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_cosh_three_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_cosh_three_term","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L60-L64","doc":"**Bar-EVEN tower three-term identity.** `cosh(a+η) + cosh(a−η) = 2 cosh η · cosh a`\n(the `c_2` sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_sinh_three_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reeb_tower_sinh_three_term","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ReebTowerJacobiAnger.lean#L53-L58","doc":"**Bar-ODD tower three-term identity.** `sinh(a+η) + sinh(a−η) = 2 cosh η · sinh a`.\nAt `a = kη` this is the recursion for the odd Reeb tower `sinh(kη)` (the `c_3`\nsector). ","signatureChunk":0}]}